<h1>Iowa Public Services Portal — a working code-sample portfolio</h1>
<p class="lead">A complete, runnable demonstration for the State of Iowa Department of Management, Division of Information Technology (DOM DoIT) Senior .NET Developer and Front-End / UI / UX Developer role. It shows the work, not just a description of it: a real ASP.NET Core application you can run, submit a sample application through, and inspect end to end.</p>
<p><strong>GitHub / Portfolio:</strong> <a href="https://github.com/PadhuPadmakshi/padmakshi-bhonagiri-portfolio">https://github.com/PadhuPadmakshi/padmakshi-bhonagiri-portfolio</a></p>

<div class="alert alert--info" role="note">
    <h2>Read this first — what this is, and what it is not</h2>
    <p>This is an <strong>independently developed portfolio demonstration</strong> created to showcase relevant capabilities for this specific opportunity. It is <strong>not</strong> a State of Iowa system, <strong>not</strong> a production service, and it holds <strong>no government security authorization</strong>. All program descriptions, applicants, and reference numbers are fictional. The author does <strong>not</strong> claim a WCAG certification or previous work for the State of Iowa — formal WCAG training is documented on her Iowa-tailored resume, but no specific certification is named or claimed — her verified background is in the <a href="#about-author">About the author</a> section below, drawn only from her resume. Accessibility here is demonstrated through code, a documented testing workflow, and honest limits (see the Accessibility page).</p>
