<h2>Try the complete user journey</h2>
<ol>
    <li><a asp-controller="Services" asp-action="Index">Browse the sample services</a> — four fictional programs with plain-language descriptions.</li>
    <li><a asp-controller="Applications" asp-action="Apply">Complete the sample Apply form</a> — with an accessible error summary, field-level errors, and error recovery. Try submitting it empty, then with a bad email, to see the recovery path.</li>
    <li>On the confirmation page, note your reference number (for example, IA-2026-0001), then <a asp-controller="Applications" asp-action="Status">check its status</a>.</li>
    <li><a asp-controller="Home" asp-action="DesignSystem">Inspect the design system</a>, including the keyboard-accessible dialog demo.</li>
</ol>
<p><a class="btn" asp-controller="Applications" asp-action="Apply">Start the sample application</a> <a class="btn btn--secondary" asp-controller="Home" asp-action="CodeSamples">Browse code samples</a></p>

<h2>Architecture at a glance</h2>
<p>Clean, layered ASP.NET Core 8, following the same separation the author has used in production healthcare, government, and financial-services work (see resume): presentation stays thin, business rules are testable without a web server, and data access is behind repositories.</p>
<table class="data-table">
    <caption>Solution layers and what each one owns</caption>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Layer / project</th><th scope="col">Owns</th><th scope="col">Does not own</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
        <tr><td><code>IowaPortal.Domain</code></td><td>Entities, enums, status rules</td><td>HTTP, SQL, file I/O</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>IowaPortal.Application</code></td><td>Validation, eligibility screening, use cases (DTOs, services)</td><td>HTTP, EF Core</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>IowaPortal.Infrastructure</code></td><td>EF Core context, repositories, seed data, parameterized ADO.NET example</td><td>Business decisions</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>IowaPortal.Web</code></td><td>MVC views, REST API controllers, middleware, Sass design system, JavaScript</td><td>Business rules</td></tr>
        <tr><td><code>IowaPortal.Tests</code></td><td>xUnit tests: validation, eligibility, service success/failure paths</td><td>—</td></tr>
    </tbody>
</table>
<p>Dependency flow is one-way: Web → Application → Domain, and Infrastructure implements Application interfaces. Nothing in Domain or Application references ASP.NET Core.</p>

