<h2>Technology stack — only what the demo actually uses</h2>
<ul>
    <li><strong>Backend:</strong> C#, .NET 8, ASP.NET Core MVC + Web API, Entity Framework Core (InMemory by default; SQL Server by configuration)</li>
    <li><strong>Front-end:</strong> Semantic HTML5, Sass/SCSS (compiled to <code>site.css</code>), vanilla JavaScript, no front-end framework in the running app</li>
    <li><strong>Tests:</strong> xUnit</li>
    <li><strong>CI/CD:</strong> Azure DevOps Pipelines (YAML in repo root)</li>
    <li><strong>Not added for keyword-matching:</strong> Angular is on the author's resume (Angular and TypeScript at Frontiers) and a representative Angular component excerpt is in <code>samples/angular/</code>, but this portal deliberately does not ship an Angular app — the DOM DoIT environment described is Bootstrap/Material moving to an enterprise design system, and a Razor + design-system implementation demonstrates that transition more directly. AWS is documented as a future-deployment note only, not wired in.</li>
</ul>

